VED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  NEGATIVE  progesterone receptor  213 fm mg cytosolic protein  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 39     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 36     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal multiple firm areas  measuring REMOVED_DATE to 0 3cm in size consistent with cysts  No frozen section performed  Firm areas submitted in A through E and the remainder of the tissue in D through J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a 22 x 16 x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen  including a 17 x 16 x 2 5cm breast and a 5 x 5 x 1 5cm axillary tail and overlying the breast is REMOVED_DATE x 6cm skin ellipse containing the entire nipple which is unremarkable  No previous biopsy site is identified and the remainder of the skin is unremarkable  7cm lateral to the nipple is a bruised retracted area  The undersurface of the specimen is composed of fibroadipose tissue and scant crispy fragments of skeletal muscle  In the area corresponding to the retracted are of the skin  there is a small puckered area of fibroadipose tissue  The undersurface of the skin ellipse is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm gritty  white tan  stellate firm mass  representative section submitted as FX 1 and saved frozen  Small fragment is sent for BRDU and ERPR  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm fragment is given to Dr  Barbara Smith s laboratory for research purposes  The closest margin is 1 5cm grossly  SECTION CODE  A C  firm areas of left breast D K  left breast L M  closest deep margin N Q  representative sections of mass R  skin S  areolar T V  lymph nodes from the axillary tail W Y  representative sections of firm fibrous lesions in the breast  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY  NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCIOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT MESTECTOMY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS LEFT PART B  RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
