c clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm tissue immediately inferior to metallic clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of possible fat necrosis  entirely submitted  immediately lateral to metallic clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm tissue immediately medial to metallic clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm tissue  superior to metallic clip   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sequential representative sections of dense fibrous tissue extending in the superior lateral posterior direction from the main lesion  medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nearest posterior margin to area of dense fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Presumed uninvolved parenchyma from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Presumed uninvolved parenchyma from the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Presumed uninvolved parenchyma from the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Presumed uninvolved parenchyma from the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue from the central region   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple  coronal section   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 possible lymph node with fatty replacement  trisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node with fatty replacement  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 lymph nodes  bisected  1 inked green   both suspicious for involvement by tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 possible lymph nodes  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast mastectomy flap   is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm ellipse of grossly unremarkable skin  excised to a depth of 0 2cm  which is serially sectioned to reveal no lesions or abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 11   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 24 08PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diag