D_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm indurated grey white to light tan mass which comes to 0 5cm from the posterior  0 8cm from the lateral  1 0cm from the medial  1 4cm from the anterior  2 0cm from the inferior  and 2 5cm from the superior margins  The remaining cut surface is 95  tan yellow and lobular with focal yellow orange discoloration predominately along the medial margin  Along the inferior aspect of the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hemorrhagic cavity  which comes to 0 7cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as follows  A  superior margin  radially sectioned B D  areas of fat necrosis E H  lesion entirely submitted I J  hemorrhagic cavity K  inferior margin  radially sectioned Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  medial margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue  with no orientation  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a predominately tan yellow lobular cut surface with focal hemorrhage and yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  Minimal fibrotic tissue is identified  and the specimen is submitted entirely as L T  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  lateral margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a predominately tan yellow lobular cut surface with focal hemorrhage and no other gross abnormality  The specimen is submitted entirely as U GG  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MEDIAL MARGIN PART C  BREAST  LEFT   LATERAL MARGIN , Unchecked.
