ression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 31   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 51 58PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  107  to chromosome 17 signals  103  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 01   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 36 06PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA  The patient has a left breast mass  Core biopsy shows malignant tumor  type unknown  Clinically  it behaves like carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  MALIGNANT SPINDLE CELL TUMOR WITH DENSE INFLAMMATORY INFILTRATE WITH FEATURES SUGGESTIVE OF FIBROBLASTIC SARCOMA  INFLAMMATORY FIBROSARCOMA    See note   NOTE  The neoplasm is composed of cytologically malignant spindle cells that are arranged haphazardly in a collagenous and myxoid stroma  In areas  the tumor is infiltrated by a dense lymphoid infiltrate  and in regions where the infiltrate is most dense  the tumor cells are polyphedral and fewer in number  Immunostains show that the tumor cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   repeated twice   weakly  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  on frozen section only  vimentin and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   nd negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cd2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cd5   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cd8   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cd68   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   ALK 1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID a  lysosyme  myeloperoxidase   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cytokeratin  smooth muscle actin  muscle actin  desmin and S 100 protein  Expression of  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  raises the possibility of a T cell lymphoma  However  the morphology  the lack of other lymphoid associated antigens and the ultrastructural features of the neoplastic cells  See EM report  are more suggestive of a fibroblastic sarcoma such as inflammatory fibrosarcoma  The tumor does not have the morphology or immunoprofile of a carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 28 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     In situ hybridization  ISH  performed on a paraffin embedded section reveals NO STAINING with an oligonucleotide probe for EBV encoded RNA  EBER   Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 16     ELECTRON MICROSCOPY Addendum     BREAST BIOPSY  MALIGNANT NEOPLASM WITH FEATURES OF FIBROBLASTIC DIFFERENTIATION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Unfortunately  the fresh tissue that was submitted for electron microscopy did not contain definitive tumor  Tissue had therefore to be retrieved from paraffin which markedly diminishes the quality of the cells  The cells do  however  seem to demonstrate features of fibroblastic differentiation  They are spindle shaped and contain dilated rough endoplasmic reticulum  Other features are difficult to interpret due to the poor quality of the tissue  Added by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 11 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast  left   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of firm  yellow  fatty soft tissue  The specimen is inked black and sectioned to reveal a 1 9cm firm well circumscribed mass surrounded by a thin rim of soft  yellow  fibrofatty tissue  The mass has a white tan  smooth cut surface and is of uniform consistency with no evidence of necrosis  One representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 1  and is kept frozen for Warren 5  A small portion of the tumor is saved for Electron Microscopy  Two sections of the tumor are fixed in B   and submitted as cassette A  The remainder of the tissue is fixed in formalin and submitted entirely as cassette B  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  MALIGNANT TUMOR  AWAITING PERMANENTS FOR CLASSIFICATION  O R  Resident  ARASH RADFAR  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
