with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm fragment of firm oval fragment of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm in greatest diameter  firm  irregular nodule that abuts the inked resection margin  This area is submitted in A and B  with the remaining tissue submitted in C  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  COMP  BREAST HEALTH CENTER REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST TISSUE  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
