S PQRI measure   99          Electronically Signed Out By Kristina M Braaten MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       CLINICAL HISTORY  Right breast cancer with positive margins now having right mastectomy  Per  CAS  history of neoadjuvant therapy     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST MASTECTOMY  RIGHT  B  BREAST BIOPSY  RIGHT SUB NIPPLE    GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     A  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nipple  sparing mastectomy with a short suture designating superior and a long suture  designating lateral  The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior margin  is inked black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm hemorrhagic cavity  in the lower inner quadrant extending to within 0 1cm of the both and anterior  and posterior margins  The surrounding tissue consists of dense gray white   rubbery  fibrous tissue  The remaining breast consists of dense gray white   focally cystic fibrous tissue admixed with minimal soft adipose tissue  There  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink lymph node identified within the lateral  tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to include closest anterior and posterior margins in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    from medial to lateral    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved breast tissue    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node  bisected     B  Received fresh  labeled  right sub nipple   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  pink gray rubbery fibrous tissue  which is submitted in toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Immunohistochemical and in situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts  General Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics