 HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm irregular portion of fibroadipose tissue with an inserted wire  A short stitch denotes the superior margin and a long stitch the lateral margin  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink  the posterior margin with black ink  the superior margin with green ink  and the inferior margin with yellow ink  The specimen is serially sectioned from the medial to the lateral aspect to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm white  fibrotic region in the vicinity of the clip seen on the specimen radiograph  Further sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm focus in the aforementioned fibrotic region which extends to 0 7cm of the anterior margin  to 0 5cm of the posterior margin  1 0cm to the superior margin  1 8cm to the inferior margin  1 8cm to the medial margin and greater than 2 0cm to the lateral margin  The remaining tissue consists predominantly of adipose tissue with a scant amount of intervening soft  white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from the medial to the lateral margin  with the biopsy site in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   with the firm nodule within the biopsy site in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin superior half cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm aggregate of unremarkable tan red fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin inferior half cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of tan red fibroadipose tissue with no orientation  Sectioning reveals unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  the specimen is entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemical Results RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING OVEREXPRESSION OF HER 2  c erb B 2  Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY   E PART C  BREAST  LEFT FINAL SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE CAVITY   EXCIS , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 27 CLINICAL DATA  85 y o  female with left breast mass  R O carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE CORE BIOPSIES  B CELL LYMPHOMA CONSISTENT WITH EXTRANODAL MARGINAL ZONE B CELL LYMPHOMA OF MUCOSA ASSOCIATED LYMPHOID TISSUE  MALT  TYPE  NOTE  There is a dense lymphoid infiltrate with focal reactive gemmal centers and a diffuse infiltrate of monomorphous small round lymphocytes  Focally  there are medium sized  irregular cells consistent with marginal zone cells  The differential diagnosis includes small lymphocytic lymphoma  follicle center lymphoma  mantle cell lymphoma and MALT type lymphoma  Immunoperoxidase stains show a  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   phenotype consistent with MALT type lymphoma  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 39                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibodies to immunoglobulin heavy and light chains there is high background  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to T lineage associated antigens   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  A  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  stain shows large irregular follicular dendritic cell meshworks  Similar staining is seen with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   With antibody to bcl 2 tumor cells are positive and germinal centers are negative  The cells are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of extranodal marginal zone B cell lymphoma and tend to exclude mantle cell  follicular and small lymphocytic lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 10 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  with no designation as to site  are 9 cores of yellow pink fibroadipose tissue ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto to cassette A  Gross Description by  Robert F Donnell Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Gerald Joseph Doyle  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY , Checked.
