OSING AND NODULAR ADENOSIS  NO DEFINITE IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  EXTENSIVE SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  NO DEFINITE IN SITU OR INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm yellow white irregular fibrofatty tissue with a short stitch designating superior  and a long stitch designating lateral and a localization wire  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x0 7 x 0 6cm tan white ovoid well circumscribed rubbery nodule abutting the superior margin  0 3cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm to both the posterior and medial margins  and greater than 1 5cm of the remaining two margins  At 0 6cm from this nodule there is an ovoid tan granular area  0 6cm from both the superior and anterior margins  0 4cm from the posterior margin and  1 5cm from the remaining margins  0 7cm inferior from this area there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan ovoid nodule which comes within 0 8cm of both the anterior and inferior margins  1 0cm from the posterior margin  15 cm from the superior margin  and  1 5cm from the remaining two margins  The remainder of the cut surface consists of yellow lobulated adipose tissue with focally yellow  hemorrhagic chalky areas  admixed with white dense fibrous tissue  Representatives sections are submitted sequentially from medial to lateral in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as labeled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   First nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Yellow chalky area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Granular area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Third nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral sections  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior half of cavity   are four yellow white irregular fragments of fibrofatty tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE On one surface  the tissue is focally tan pink to white and rubbery  No lesions or masses are identified  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast inferior half of cavity   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm yellow white irregular  fragmented fibrofatty tissue  No lesions or masses are identified  The specimen is submitted entirely in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION , Unchecked.
