OVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment with localizing wire and accompanying roentgenogram  This specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm moderately delineated  tan  rubbery nodule abutting an inked resection margin  Representative section frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is sent for ERPR and BRDU  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through F  with the lesion found in A and B  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  CONSISTENT WITH CARCINOMA WITH ATYPICAL FEATURES INCLUDING LOBULAR PATTERN AND QUESTION FOCAL AREAS OF MUCIN PRODUCTION  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Wiley Souba  MD PART   BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
