d or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary sentinel lymph node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node candidate which is bivalved and entirely submitted for frozen as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received are five containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  left mastectomy skin flap   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm linear portion of tan brown grossly unremarkable skin  The resection margin is inked black and a representative section is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled  right mastectomy skin flap   are two linear portions of tan brown  grossly unremarkable skin averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The resection margin is inked black and a representative section is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan brown skin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 3 0cm curvilinear  well healed scar present approximately 1 0cm from the nipple between the 6 and 9 o clock position  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  On the posterior surface there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm exposed biopsy cavity  The specimen is serially sectioned along medial to lateral axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm biopsy cavity with incontinuity with the exposed cavity in the posterior surface and lies 2 0cm from overlying inked margin  The biopsy cavity approximately lies beneath the overlying well healed scar on anterior surface between 6 and 9 o clock position  The breast parenchyma surrounding the biopsy cavity is tan white  firm to hard and nodular  which is palpated for lymph nodes  The remaining breast parenchyma contains diffuse tan white rubbery breast tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  biopsy cavity to include posterior inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  fibrous breast parenchyma  upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  fibrous breast parenchyma  inner lower quadrant  Received fresh  labeled with  left breast   is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 6 o clock  The anterior surface contains REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm tan brown skin ellipse which contains REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 2 5cm tan white  linear well healed scar present 2 0cm from the areola  approximately between 12 and 2 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned along medial to lateral axis to reveal REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan white  stellate scar approximately between 12 and 1 o clock  positioned beneath the overlying linear well healed scar which grossly abuts the posterior inked margin and lies 0 5cm from the anterior inked margin  Adjacent to the scar  is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity lined by tan pink smooth glistening to focally tan brown granular lining  The biopsy cavity grossly abuts the posterior inked margin and lies 0 6cm from the overlying anterior margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the scar and the biopsy cavity is focally nodular  The remaining breast parenchyma contains tan white  focally nodular and cystic fibrous breast parenchyma  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated