ults of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  indicated with a long stitch lateral  short stitch superior  The specimen is inked black  superior overinked yellow  posterior overinked blue  and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm hard white mass  0 2cm from the superior anterior margin and 0 4cm from the posterior margin  Tumor is submitted entirely in cassettes A through E  Representative sample of uninvolved breast in F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast additional anterior superior margin  are fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring 3 x 2 x 0 9cm in aggregate  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette H through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes K through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a 6 x 6 x 3 5cm piece of fatty tissue containing lymph nodes  Multiple lymph nodes were found  The bigger nodes are bisected and half o