Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 01 CLINICAL DATA  Breast lesion biopsied on the outside and reviewed here                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1 INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   SEE NOTE   2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ARISING IN ASSOCIATION WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES WITH REACTIVE FOLLICULAR HYPERPLASIA  THE LYMPH NODES APPEAR FREE OF CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunostains for keratin will be reported in an addendum  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA NON SENTINEL   EXCISION  REACTIVE FOLLICULAR HYPERPLASIA  CARCINOMA IS NOT SEEN   NOTE  All margins appear free of tumor  No definite blood vascular invasion is seen  The tumor displays neuroendocrine features  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 32                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  LEFT   THE GRIMELIUS STAIN AND CHROMAGRANIN IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAIN ARE FOCALLY POSITIVE FURTHER SUGGESTING NEUROENDOCRINE DIFFERENTIATION  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  SENTINEL   IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS FOR KERATIN ARE NEGATIVE  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 35     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm fragment of oriented breast parenchyma with a short stitch indicating the superior margin and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The tissue is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm dumbbell shaped  stellate  tan white lesion with a gritty cut surface present 0 8cm from the deep margin  0 7cm from the medial margin  and 0 8cm from the anterior margin  1 2cm from the superior margin  3 7cm from the lateral margin  and 2 4cm from the inferior margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Tumor and anterior margin B  Tumor and deep margin C  Tumor and medial margin D  Representative section of mass Labeled  left axillary sentinel node x2  are two fragments of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The larger fragment is sectioned to reveal a single lymph node  2 0cm in greatest dimension  This lymph node is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes E and F  The smaller fragment of tissue is sectioned to reveal a single lymph node  0 8cm in greatest dimension  submitted entirely in cassette G  Labeled  left axillary non sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue sectioned to reveal a single lymph node  1 0cm in greatest dimension  submitted entirely in cassette H  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA NON SENTINEL   EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
