ns of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue with a stitch marking the anterior lateral margin as denoted by the surgeon  The specimen is inked black and the anterior lateral half has been overinked green  It is sectioned to reveal a a firm area 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The firm area is submitted in A  with the remainder submitted in B through I  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  lateral margin tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of breast tissue that is inked and submitted in its entirety in cassette J  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  SMALL FIRM AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL MARGIN   EXCISION , Unchecked.
