red the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  1  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1cm piece of breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable parenchyma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette D through M  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue  2  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of breast tissue  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm firm  white  ill defined nodule  Representative sections of the nodule are submitted in cassettes A through C  Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST TISSUE  1   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  2   LEFT BREAST TISSUE  2   SMALL LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   1   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  2   EXCISION , Unchecked.
