imen with a long stitch lateral and a short stitch superior  On the anterior surface of the breast  there is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm nipple areolar complex  The anterior of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral  to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast parenchyma with areas of fibrocystic change  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from central portion of breast  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 331 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm right total mastectomy specimen oriented with a long stitch lateral and a short stitch superior  On the anterior surface  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm nipple areolar complex  There is a palpable mass at 5 o clock in the central breast region  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior inked black  and the specimen serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm firm pink tan  ill defined mass near the lower inner quadrant of breast at approximately 5 o clock which approaches to within 0 2cm of the deep margin  and approaches to within 0 6cm of the anterior margin  There is an area of hemorrhage in the mass consistent with prior biopsy cavity  A portion of the mass is sent for tumor bank  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is notable for areas of dense fibrocystic changes  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm pink  ill defined nodular area with a central scar consistent with prior biopsy cavity at approximately 12 o clock in the upper breast  No other masses are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to nearest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections through mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section through ill defined slightly firm nodule at 12 o clock   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of unremarkable  uninvolved fibrofatty breast tissue between 12 o clock lesion and 5 o clock lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma distant from lesions   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Potential lymph node  Received fresh  labeled  right breast additional margin  superficial to mass   is an unoriented  4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right axillary contents   is an REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 1 7cm aggregate of fibroadipose tissue in which multiple lymph nodes are identified  Specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two potential lymph nodes  both bisected  one of which is inked black   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 bisected lymph nodes  1 of which is inked black   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Five potential lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 potential lymph nodes  intact   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 potential intact lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 potential lymph nodes  intact  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT AXILLA SENTINEL NODE   REMOVED_CASE_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  AWAIT SENTINEL NODE WORKUP  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2   RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL NODE   REMOVED_CASE_ID    METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 LYMPH NODE  1 1   0 2 CM   MACRO METASTASIS   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Sunday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 39 50PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or correct