Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 52 CLINICAL DATA  Mass on mammography                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  AND FOCALLY TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  SKIN  RIGHT CHEST   EXCISION  DERMAL NEVUS  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone recptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of unoriented fatty tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a white  gritty lesion measuring 0 9cm in greatest dimension  0 7cm from the closest margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen section  1  now A  The nodule with closest margin is in B  The remainder of the nodule is in C and D  The remainder of the tissue is mostly fatty with streaks of white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are in E and F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right chest lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm soft polypoid pinkish gray tissue  inked  bisected and fully submitted in G  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  SKIN  RIGHT CHEST   EXCISION , Unchecked.
