gins  This second suspicious area is 1 3cm inferoposterior to the first  Finally there is a third REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm cyst which abuts the posterosuperior margin and comes to 1 7cm of the inferior  1 7cm of the anterior  and greater than 2 0cm of both the medial and lateral margins  This third lesion is 1 3cm from the first and 1 4cm of the second lesions  No definitive previous biopsy site is identified  and the remaining cut surface consists of 80  tan yellow adipose and 20  dense gray white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted from medial to lateral as follows  A  Medial margin  radial   B C  Representative fibrous tissue from medial half of specimen  D E  Full thickness section with suspicious areas  1 and  3 as D and  2 as E  F G  Full thickness section with suspicious areas  1 and  3 as F and  2 as G  H  Suspicious areas  1 and  3  I  Representative fibrous tissue from lateral half of specimen  J  Lateral margin  radial   The remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from medial to lateral as K Q with 2 full thickness sections bisected in K L  M N  superior margins in K  M   Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
