Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  16 AUG 93 at 15 21 CLINICAL DATA  Right mammographic abnormality                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  85   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    NOTE  The carcinoma measures 0 7cm in greatest dimension  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Intraductal carcinoma is present at the margin  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  18 AUG 93 at 17 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 AUG 93 at 09 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 4cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm with ill defined borders grossly within 0 1cm of one inked margin  The lesion was too small to freeze  The lesion is submitted in A and B  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in C through G  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   SMALL SUSPICIOUS AREA  NOT LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  James Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE , Unchecked.
