ectomy specimen with attached axillary tail  There is an overlying central REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm white skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm nipple areola complex  The nipple stands erect with a length of 2 0cm  No identifiable scars are seen grossly  The entire specimen is inked black  sectioning reveals predominantly dense white fibrous tissue with and a 1cm hard irregular white yellow nodular mass is noticed in the lateral half of the specimen at 0 8cm from the deep margin  There is a region of diffuse fibrosis with scattered calcifications and cysts measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm and abuting the deep inked resection margin  The majority of the gritty parenchyma is located laterally  1 5cm from the axillary tail and medially  2 7cm from the medial margin  Grossly it cannot be determined if the gritty parenchyma involves the nipple  The remaining parenchyma uninvolved by this dense area of gritty fibrosis is predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue  Section code  A  Central section of gritty fibrosis in relation to deep margin  B  Lateral section of gritty fibrosis in relation to deep margin  C  Medial section of gritty fibrosis in relation to deep margin  D  Gritty fibrosis from medial aspect in relation to anterior margin  overinked blue   E  Gritty fibrosis from lateral aspect in relation to deep margin  black  and anterior margin  inked blue   F  Section of nipple and subjacent parenchyma  J  Representative section of unremarkable medial parenchyma  N O  Nodular mass  P R  Representative sections  The attached axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm from which multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  A representative section from each lymph node is submitted in cassettes H M  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNO